rom a  family of actors all of them quite  handsome  his father stellan has also been  physically transformed for roles like  bootstrap bill turner and the pirates of  the caribbean films it's a testimony to  the power of makeup that you'd never  look at pennywise and the barnacle-faced  bill and realize they're actually father  and son  darth maul the vermillion villain from  the star wars universe was played by ray  park  a martial artist and actor who got his  start as a stunt double in 1997's mortal  kombat annihilation  since then he's appeared in a number of  action-oriented parts with maul being  the most famous  park loved playing him one reason being  that becoming the character through the  magic of makeup gave him a real rush  the sith lord's appearance instantly  communicates that he's a formidable  presence and a major menace  his unique look combined with park's  particular set of skills resulted in a  villain who truly terrified every star  wars fan in the world  during a 2019 interview with sci-fi wire  park recalled a directive he received  from producer rick mccallum  from rick it was like now rey i want you  to be mean i want you to scare every  child in america and around the world  you're gonna be bad this turned out to  be an inspired casting choice as park  was able to use his martial arts  background to battle in a lightsaber  fight grounded in very little script  direction  his face might not be recognizable in  this role but his moves definitely are  when dave chase isn't climbing out of  the tv as she did in the 2002 horror  classic the ring  she's a considerably less terrifying  figure in fact she's even worked as a  model her tv and movie parts have  definitely been on the darker side  though her first major live-action role  was the 2001 psychological thriller  donnie darko as the title character's  little sister  and then starting in 2006 she played the  sociopathic rhonda volmer on the hbo  series big love  in the ring chase played sa