n  2000's x-men  is how her blue makeup was able to stick  to her it wasn't easy as her first  screen test required a jaw-dropping 12  hours in the makeup chair which was cut  down to a still staggering 9 for the  second movie  2003's x2 x-men united and finally down  to 7 for 2006's x-men the last stand  that all sounds particularly grueling  even by hollywood standards  in fact it seems like it would require  mutant powers for an actor to get  through it  especially when you consider that  romaine had to be made up and on set at  9am  as for the rest of her career she's had  plenty of other roles that don't require  quite so much detailed preparation  you may have seen her for example as  number one on star trek discovery or as  alexis mead on ugly betty and she's also  hosted skin wars a competition show that  centers around insane body painting  challenges  she certainly knows something about that  it's not just the bald head and the  missing nose that make ray finds so  unrecognizable as harry potter nemesis  lord voldemort it's also the fact that  the actor is rather striking in real  life and you don't have to look far for  proof  as he's appeared in a number of films in  which his natural face is fully visible  though voldemort's visage is decidedly  different from fines  the transformational process wasn't as  complicated as you might expect  temporary tattoos false teeth and fake  fingernails were all it took to turn  this talented thespian into the most  despised villain in the wizarding world  over in the muggle world you've probably  seen finds in a variety of flicks in  1993 he infamously played war criminal  ammun gert in schindler's list which  earned him an oscar nomination for best  supporting actor  then 1996's the english patient led to  another round of accolades and more  recently he's appeared in the likes of  clash of the titans the grand budapest  hotel and the james bond franchise  starting with 2012's skyfall check out  one of our newest v